 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Two curves",
   "text": "For two vectors of magnitudes A and B, the **dot product** is \\( AB\\cos\\theta \\) and the **magnitude of the cross product** is \\( AB\\sin\\theta \\). The graph shows \\( \\cos\\theta \\) and \\( \\sin\\theta \\), the parts multiplied by AB.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 0,
      "th": 30
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Parallel: θ = 0°",
   "text": "At 0° cos θ = 1 (dot product is maximum, AB) and sin θ = 0 (cross product is zero).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 1
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "th": 0
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 1800
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Perpendicular: θ = 90°",
   "text": "At 90° cos θ = 0 (dot product is zero) and sin θ = 1 (cross product is maximum, AB).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 2
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "th": 90
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 2500
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "The ratio is tan θ",
   "text": "Divide the two: \\( |\\vec A\\times\\vec B| / (\\vec A\\cdot\\vec B) = \\tan\\theta \\). This is how problems such as “the cross product is √3 times the dot product” give θ = 60°.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 3
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "th": 60
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 2200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Where are they equal?",
   "text": "\\( |\\cos\\theta| = |\\sin\\theta| \\Rightarrow \\tan\\theta = 1 \\Rightarrow \\theta = 45^\\circ \\). The dashed curve is |cos θ|.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 4
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "th": 45
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 2200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "135° works too",
   "text": "For an obtuse angle the dot product is negative, but its **magnitude** equals the cross product at 135°. The textbook MCQ offers only 45°, so the answer is 45° (flag F5).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "lv": 5
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "th": 135
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 2600
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "readouts": [
